From: AlexanderNyr <131390634+AlexanderNyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 11:00:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] W6 update: navigation and networking

WEBVIEW_PLAN.md phase W6:
- wv_url.{h,c}: URL parser + relative resolver (32 host checks)
- wv_http.{h,c}: HTTP/1.1 GET + Host:, header parser, chunked decoder
  (chunked == plain bytes, the plan's gate), growing response buffer
  (8KB -> 512KB cap, diagnosed refusal) -- 69 host checks incl. 100KB
  through 2KB appends
- links in the display list (link_off); hit-testing; address bar +
  Back/Go chrome; 8-entry history; https refusal page (plan D6)
- QEMU gate test_webview_net.sh: host server serves /, /page2.html,
  /chunked, /big (100KB); guest fetches home, follows link 0 -> page2,
  back -> home, refuses https with the explanation, decodes chunked,
  receives 100KB in full -- 11 assertions, no internet needed
- test hooks: /tmp/webview.url + /tmp/webview.steps (| separated),
  written before run webview (the init shell blocks on a running child)
- kernel TCP note: legacy path can drop the last bytes on FIN
  (259-byte body arrived as 256); web view renders the partial body
- bugs found: init shell splits ';' (steps separator -> '|'); shell
  does not strip quotes; shell blocks on run (hooks before start)
- webview.elf ~188 KB; make test-unit green; both integration tests pass
